# scripts/spec-vocabs/clj-table.vocab -- rows are repl statements, or slim
# assertion rows:
# form \t value \t out [\t expect]
# `include` splices another vocabulary's directives in first, so a table
# case is a repl case: the generator rewrites each row into repl statement
# lines (`;=> value`, `;; out: out`, `;; expect: fail`) and feeds them
# through the clj-repl rules below.
#
# A `|!` slim row (FitNesse SLIM decision-table style) is NOT rewritten to
# repl lines: it stays a row of cells and is emitted as a slim-check! call
# against those cells. The runner annotates the row inline (pass/fail per
# cell with actuals), FitNesse-style, so a re-rendered wiki shows the diff
# where the claim lives.
include clj-repl
row => form
slim-row => (slim-check! "{id}" {table} {row})
